locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"1eaeb82366c9f219e43ed918ed6abb647a43667035c3db3f764939200475d845\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bc1fb4f05052ede27f5a14e74c445621fe766a337b12fd92d01ce0ddbc328e59\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Han Kang born Gwangju South Korea author\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_35b1d2c7254d4325bb918b58"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d33\",\"document_chars\":5590,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e3\",\"sha256\":\"2d508167d68898ab9a94c04692e5dd49383dedb168f97d4bee80fdb0b10e35ba\",\"snapshot\":\"cf73f3198b61e06ea1409d0fa598f3ca5393950bb56774813f67f99bb8d90e1d\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: 'My novels explore human suffering': Nobel Prize winner Han Kang writes with empathy for vulnerable lives\\ndate: 2024-10-10\\n---\\nSouth Korean writer Han Kang has won the 2024 Nobel Prize for Literature, \\\"for her intense poetic prose that confronts historical traumas and exposes the fragility of human life\\\". The 53-year-old is the first South Korean writer to win the prize, and only the 18th woman (of 121 winners to date). She is also a musician, and interested in visual art.\\n\\nHer best known novel, The Vegetarian (published in Korea in 2007), was her first to be translated into English, in 2015. It won the Man Booker International Prize in 2016, with the prize split between Han Kang and her translator, Deborah Smith.\\n\\nAt the time, Smith's translation sparked fervid debates about its accuracy. But this is the beauty of literary translation as an act of creation: it's an imaginative exercise, not a literal one, and Han Kang has stood by her translator.\\n\\nHan Kang has published six works in English so far. The Vegetarian was her international breakout. Then there was Human Acts, The White Book, Europa and Greek Lessons. The short work Convalescence was published in a bilingual edition in 2013.\\n\\nHer latest novel We Do Not Part, about a writer researching the 1948-49 Jeju uprising (against the Cold War division of the Korean peninsula) and its impact on the family of her friend will be published in 2025.\\n\\nTaking up space in the world\\n\\nA macabre tale of daily brutality, The Vegetarian is a novel in three acts, and follows the choice of a \\\"completely unremarkable\\\" woman to give up meat, triggering a spiral of unprecedented abuse from family members. While they claim to be thinking of her health, actually they oppose her non-conformism. Eventually, considering herself to be a plant, she refuses any nourishment apart from water and the sun's rays.\\n\\nThe Nobel committee praised Han's \\\"physical empathy for the vulnerable, often female lives\\\" of her characters.\\n\\nGreek Lessons is narrated by a woman who has lost her mother, her son (to the custody of his father) and is losing her ability to speak, and a man who is losing his connection to place and family, and his eyesight. The man teaches ancient Greek; the woman becomes his student.\\n\\nLike much of Han Kang's other work, Greek Lessons explores, through evocative and laconic prose, the fragile and unstable space between what can be expressed and shared, and what remains incommunicable, beyond the possibility of words. It shows the power of the human search for connection: even among, or perhaps because of, grief and loss.\\n\\nReviewing Greek Lessons, The Guardian concluded: \\\"thank goodness Han Kang's literary voice takes up space in the world in the way her female characters struggle to\\\".\\n\\nThe autobiographical The White Book – dazzling, touching, and at times mystical – was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize in 2018. It is an art book, an extended poem and a graphically white book about all \"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false,\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":3000,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"han\",\"kang\",\"vegetarian\",\"translated\",\"into\",\"international\",\"booker\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":12.200185,\"selected_block\":[490,736],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":0},\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_1ae65602f1f84c10bf5c6eb0"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d33\",\"document_chars\":5590,\"end\":5590,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"1d57ba6fe1ec2500b762edaa594992659fe35a6130ff2876a3ab9ec0b1d2ad3d\",\"snapshot\":\"cf73f3198b61e06ea1409d0fa598f3ca5393950bb56774813f67f99bb8d90e1d\",\"start\":3585,\"text\":\"Han Kang composes this meditative, transcendental book while on a writers' residency in Warsaw. The white of the snow mixes with the white of memory.\\n\\nWriting becomes a purifying act: reconstructing her sister's death means starting to live. The resulting reflections follow the rhythm of prayer, perhaps a secular, yet deeply human prayer. The only way to mourn, and at the same time continue to live ethically, is the flash of memory, in its endless fragments.\\n\\nA nation's mourning\\n\\nIn Human Acts, this autobiographical mourning becomes the mourning of an entire nation.\\n\\nHuman Acts narrates the massacre in Gwangju, Kang's birthplace of May 1980, when hundreds, perhaps thousands, of citizens and university students, protesting against the authoritarian regime of South Korea's \\\"most vilified\\\" military dictator, Chun Doo-Hwan, were murdered by the army.\\n\\nParadoxically, precisely in the midst of these brutal acts what is most valuable emerges: solidarity, dignity, the strength to continue – and above all, the great responsibility of surviving and remembering.\\n\\n\\\"My novels explore human suffering,\\\" Han Kang once said. When she wrote about the Gwangju massacre, she was \\\"aware that readers should, in turn, be prepared […] to experience such suffering firsthand themselves\\\".\\n\\nThe ethical scope of the novel counteracts the collective amnesia imposed by censorship. It makes room for a chorale – a sacred song – in which the living are confused with the dead, the present with the past, memory with censorship, the word with the ineffability of a violence that is supposedly inhuman. Could surviving perhaps be a form of silent consent?\\n\\nBut as in The White Book, the silence crumbles in the writing, becoming too loud to bear. The role of the writer is to continue to create, remember, communicate even the incommunicable, despite it all. Even in shreds. Even silence. Even when humanity seems to fail us.\\n\\nFor this – and much more – Han Kang richly deserves this year's Nobel Prize for Literature.\",\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"},{\"document\":\"d5\",\"document_chars\":27249,\"end\":27249,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"344484bdc42ae9da871c59569e92bd28f735887242cc377e73ef6f0a04d23171\",\"snapshot\":\"25e42c9d9629a06063929aefe4e8f050cac2c095d797b7476410c1a6fe277c5a\",\"start\":25007,\"text\":\"A Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian writer, either written in English or translated into English, and published in the previous calendar year.\\n\\nFor many years, as part of The Times Literature Festival in Cheltenham, a Booker event was held on the last Saturday of the festival. Four guest speakers/judges debated a shortlist of four books from a given year from before the introduction of the Booker Prize, and a winner was chosen. Unlike the real Booker Prize (1969 through 2014), writers from outside the Commonwealth were also considered. In 2008, the winner for 1948 was Alan Paton's Cry, the Beloved Country, beating Norman Mailer's The Naked and the Dead, Graham Greene's The Heart of the Matter and Evelyn Waugh's The Loved One. In 2015, the winner for 1915 was Ford Madox Ford's The Good Soldier, beating The Thirty-Nine Steps (John Buchan), Of Human Bondage (W. Somerset Maugham), Psmith, Journalist (P. G. Wodehouse) and The Voyage Out (Virginia Woolf).Haslam, Sara (13 October 2015), \\\"Ford's The Good Soldier Wins The Cheltenham Booker 1915 at 2015 Festival\\\". Ford Madox Oxford Society. Retrieved 27 November 2016.\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* Baillie Gifford Prize (formerly the Samuel Johnson Prize)\\n* Commonwealth Writers Prize\\n* Costa Book Awards\\n* German Book Prize (Deutscher Buchpreis)\\n* Giller Prize (known as the Scotiabank Giller Prize from 2005 to 2023)\\n* Governor General's Awards\\n* Grand Prix of Literary Associations\\n* Miles Franklin Award\\n* Prix Goncourt\\n* Russian Booker Prize\\n* List of British literary awards\\n* List of literary awards\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nFurther reading\\n\\n* \\n* \\n* \\n\\nExternal links\\n\\n* (The Booker Prize)\\n* (Booker Prize Foundation)\\n* The Booker Prize Archive at Oxford Brookes University\\n* A primer on the Man Booker Prize and critical review of literature\\n\\nCategory:1968 establishments in the United Kingdom\\nCategory:Awards established in 1968\\nCategory:Booker authors' division\\nCategory:British fiction awards\\nCategory:English-language literary awards\\nCategory:Oxford Brookes University\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\",\"e2\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":188,\"backend_calls\":92,\"model_calls\":9,\"output_reservation\":46945},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... The case of the hub city of Asian culture, Gwangju, South Korea. Doctor of Philosophy, 2015.\\n\\nHenderson, Calen Barnett. The Korean microlensing telescope n\",\"title\":\"https://easc.osu.edu/degrees/theses-dissertations\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d106\"},\"ref\":\"d106\",\"snippet\":\" ... Episode 18\\tMarch 21, 2017\\t26.6% (2nd)\\t30.3% (1st)\\t28.3% (1st)\\t29.7% (1st)\\nThe battle comes to a head, as Kang Jun Hyeok comes clean to Park Jeong Woo and C\",\"title\":\"https://drama.fandom.com/wiki/Defendant\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d105\"},\"ref\":\"d105\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hwang is also known to have grown close to children's writer Kang So-cheon (1915-1963), with whom he shared a sense of belonging as a writer who had migrat\",\"title\":\"https://www.korea.net/NewsFocus/Culture/view?articleId=133876\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d104\"},\"ref\":\"d104\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Vegetarian by Han Kang\\n\\nThis novel grew out of Kang's 1997 short story, The Fruit of My Woman, in which the protagonist literally turns into a plant. M\",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/oct/18/top-10-allegories\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d103\"},\"ref\":\"d103\",\"snippet\":\" ... A haunted and haunting reverie.\\\"\\n\\nHan Kang, tr. Deborah Smith, The Vegetarian (188 pages)\\n\\nThe Vegetarian has come under scrutiny for its translation, and \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-50-best-contemporary-novels-under-200-pages/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d102\"},\"ref\":\"d102\",\"snippet\":\" ... The 2022 International Booker Prize Shortlist\\nauthor: Geetanjali Shree; Daisy Rockwell\\ndate: 2022-06-24\\n---\\nThe International Booker Prize celebrates the b\",\"title\":\"https://fivebooks.com/best-books/the-best-of-world-literature-the-2022-international-booker-prize-shortlist-frank-wynne/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d101\"},\"ref\":\"d101\",\"snippet\":\" ... Moors Last Sigh\\\"\\n\\n- \\\"The Satanic Verses\\\"\\n\\n- \\\"Two Years Eight Months and Twenty-Eight Nights\\\"\\n\\n- Notable Family Members:\\n\\n- spouse Padma Lakshmi\\n\\nWho is Sal\",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Salman-Rushdie\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d100\"},\"ref\":\"d100\",\"snippet\":\" ... In a letter dated April 6, 1904, he writes, \\\"Either Miss Hopkins will follow our suggestions...and put live matter into the magazine, eliminating anything,\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Colored_American_Magazine\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":0,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":7,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":7,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}